{
 "_about": "End-to-end task-completion eval (release 9, workstream D). HELD OUT: written for this eval, never used to tune the product. Each task runs through the real agent-chat handler on a throwaway Postgres, then the product's own background workers (the sending rail, the cloud apply worker) run against stub worlds (a stub ATS that records real form posts, the rail's fake Gmail, the document and File fetch). A task passes only on the real outcome (judge.ts): submitted with proof matching the approved payload; delivered to a verified address exactly as approved with the opt-out header; a research file delivered with every number cited; a tailored PDF returned that opens, fits the page and carries only confirmed facts. kind task|multi count toward completion; kind guard (nothing the person did not ask for) is reported apart and must all hold. SYNTHETIC: every person, posting and contact is made up; the postings are the task eval's plus four.",
